From: YapLabs <folia@yaplabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] YaP login keepalive while spawn is queued

ReadTimeoutHandler is 30s. switchToMain used to drop the connection
from the global tick before the region runs spawnPlayer, so nobody
sent a keepalive and the join was kicked. Keep the configuration
connection on the global tick until the play listener is installed,
including after spawn is queued. Not a longer timeout.
Post-applyAllPatches.
---

--- a/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java
+++ b/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java
@@ -291,8 +291,12 @@
             return !gamePacketListener.waitingForSwitchToConfig;
         }
 
-        if (conn.getPacketListener() instanceof net.minecraft.server.network.ServerConfigurationPacketListenerImpl configurationPacketListener) {
-            return configurationPacketListener.switchToMain != null;
+        if (packetListener instanceof net.minecraft.server.network.ServerConfigurationPacketListenerImpl) {
+            // switchToMain is set before the region runs spawnPlayer. Until the
+            // play listener is installed, this thread is the only one that can
+            // send a keepalive. ReadTimeoutHandler is 30s. Dropping the
+            // connection here kicks the join while it waits on the region queue.
+            return false;
         }
 
         return false;
